    "category": "skill",
    "description": {
      "value": "<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Your infamy and physique can terrify creatures to your advantage. When you @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.tHCqgwjtQtzNqVvd]{Coerce} or @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.2u915NdUyQan6uKF]{Demoralize} a target that knows of you or can see you, you can use Strength in place of Charisma for your proficiency bonus.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">In addition, when you are able to physically menace a target, directly or indirectly, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to your Intimidation check when your Strength or Charisma modifier is +3. This increases to a +2 circumstance bonus when the modifiers are +5 or higher and you are a master in intimidation.</p>",
